\lambda )={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =-7A-17I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-83396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-83396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-83396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-17A-7I"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e