2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ then ${A}^{3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,x$ | $+$ | $1$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-x-20\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\,\\,}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | $-$ | ${x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $20x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | ${x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $20x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | ${x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $x$ | $-$ | $20$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $21x$ | $+$ | $20$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{3}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =q(x)p(x)+(21x+20),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)=x+1.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{3}=q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =21A+20I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-20A-21I"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-21A+20I"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "20A+21I"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "21A+20I"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "21A-20I"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85931" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "21A+20I"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]$\nand $f(x)={x}^{21}-16{x}^{19}+6x-3$, find $f(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda ) \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{19}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-16\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{21}\\,-\\,16{x}^{19}\\,+\\,6x\\,\\,-\\,\\,3}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{21}$ | $-$ | $16{x}^{19}$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $6x$ | $-$ | $3$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(6x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{19}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(6A-3I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(6A-3I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(6A-3I) \\\\  & =6A-3I \\\\  & =6[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -24\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}21 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15cb6b92d182e5278ecaaaa3821a9a850fd84daaabbb087c401a2c99368d7107" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 \\\\ 72 & -27\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -72\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}27 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -21\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/state.json" "file_sha256" "53fd71314705cc27c121d2e590ddcf2bf95e3f37fe26ee975b9f6452012f9fd1" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/assets/cb48b48ef82e5d6cfe903488e80a8cbd48e286c864ba387450e01430e718d77c.png) find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5894.json" "file_sha256" "d7f90c3ad3c27488da5873f508cb16d0ff771495af6ce17339eaeb9281acd9f0" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda),$ i.e., the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2 = \\textrm{tr}(A)= 9+(-6)=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5894.json" "file_sha256" "d7f90c3ad3c27488da5873f508cb16d0ff771495af6ce17339eaeb9281acd9f0" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $\\textrm{tr}(A)=-4$ and $\\textrm{det}(A)=-18.$ If $A^2 = xA + yI$ for constants $x$ and $y,$ then find the value of $x+y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5511.json" "file_sha256" "bcb30d0842bf6dad542b6e92bfab23d81a797bcb62bd66e8bb61a4d77471566d" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by \n\n$$\np(\\lambda)=\\lambda^2-\\textrm{tr}(A)\\lambda+\\textrm{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =-4A+18I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y = -4+18 = 14.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5511.json" "file_sha256" "bcb30d0842bf6dad542b6e92bfab23d81a797bcb62bd66e8bb61a4d77471566d" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/assets/b2240a11f1760050914a9c02554e0b7e86cd84d420fb437a43d95b474103b26c.png) and $A^{-1}=pI+qA$, find the value of $p+q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5510.json" "file_sha256" "85b381ca8578253e424c03b568f177c63b6aff52d8cc219ed95d3a26ff8e11b4" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-8-\\lambda  & -9 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-8-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )+54 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}+A-2I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by $A^{-1}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}+A-2I) & =O \\\\ A+I-2{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2}A+\\frac{1}{2}I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\dfrac{1}{2},$ $q=\\dfrac{1}{2},$ and \n\n$$\np+q=\\dfrac{1}{2}+\\dfrac{1}{2}=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5510.json" "file_sha256" "85b381ca8578253e424c03b568f177c63b6aff52d8cc219ed95d3a26ff8e11b4" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/assets/308850190e8483ae48e8179585c01f1805e6caf92e4d4254c996bd0ffa800427.png) and $f(x) = x^{12} -x^{10} +2x-1,$ find $f(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5512.json" "file_sha256" "d035f562be78a1af73bcfd412f1e2eb23987f3f076f7ca9d5191f9b49c508a25" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 3 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )+15 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\:\\:x^{10}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x^2-1\\:$ | $\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{x^{12} \\, - \\, x^{10}  +  2x  -  1 {\\phantom{|}} }$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x^{12}$ | $-$ | $x^{10}$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $2x$ | $-$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{10}({x}^{2}-1)+(2x-1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x) = x^{10}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A) = q(A)p(A)+(2A-I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(2A-I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(2A-I) \\\\  & =2A-I \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/example-5512.json" "file_sha256" "d035f562be78a1af73bcfd412f1e2eb23987f3f076f7ca9d5191f9b49c508a25" "basis" 1867 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14058184/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-83393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =10-24 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52afb5275bd0959a2d515d3f40a045f29dca7f07c8dc62c8195a0317cd10c970"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-14"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "34"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-83393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-140519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-140519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=4+1=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-140519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52afb5275bd0959a2d515d3f40a045f29dca7f07c8dc62c8195a0317cd10c970"} {"question" "q-140519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-140519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-140519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-85923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -3\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-85923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-3)-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-15-10 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-85923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52afb5275bd0959a2d515d3f40a045f29dca7f07c8dc62c8195a0317cd10c970"} {"question" "q-85923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-85923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-15"] ["math" "-25"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-85923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-25"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{aligned}],$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=-12+3=-9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52afb5275bd0959a2d515d3f40a045f29dca7f07c8dc62c8195a0317cd10c970"} {"question" "q-38720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38720" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{5} \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52afb5275bd0959a2d515d3f40a045f29dca7f07c8dc62c8195a0317cd10c970"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{9}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-38703" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.typ