 "{A}^{2}-3A+16I"] ["math" "{A}^{2}-3A+6I"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-85924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{A}^{2}-3A+16I"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-83398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $\\text{tr}(A)=-14$ and $\\text{det}(A)=-36.$ Then, ${A}^{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-83398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by \n\n$$\np(\\lambda )={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =-14A+36I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "51da58a67643ee915b8cacd53c1ca2a82be583c60f64763f09ea4d3eb6812ebb"} {"question" "q-83398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52afb5275bd0959a2